 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Shu'ayb: no motif, figure or drop; the plates start after his name. Geometric for «اعبدوا الله ما لكم من إله غيره», wheat for «بخير», scales for «أوفوا المكيال والميزان بالقسط» (trade, not the Mizan; nothing on the negated «ولا تنقصوا»), light for «بقيت الله». The plan's «الوفاء بالكيل» restated two passage words. STAGING v4: Madyan in a market street by day (84-85: measure and weight), as in 7_85-86. Shu'ayb is a blue drop labelled Shu'ayb (no plate on his name, no close-up or pan on his drop); his people three faceless men in dark robes (the series' sign for a group). c1 (84): wide on the narration (84:1-4); Shu'ayb speaks to them (84:5, 84:21); geometric for worship Allah, you have no god but Him (84:7-13); the camera on them for do not decrease the measure (84:15; nothing is acted inside the prohibition); a wheat plate for I see you in prosperity (84:20, As-Sa'di: much blessing); the camera on them for the warning of the encompassing Day (84:23). c2 (85-86): a scales plate for give full measure and weight in justice (85:2-5; worldly weights, not the Mizan); nobody is shown measuring, giving short or giving full (a command to them is not acted as obeyed). Three townspeople (light robes, the people of 85:8) stand by the stalls: the camera on them for do not deprive people of their things (85:8), on the men in dark robes for do not spread corruption (85:13). Geometric (not light) for what Allah leaves you (86:1-4, the Name follows at once); no gesture inside the condition (86:5-7); Shu'ayb speaks again for I am not a guardian over you (86:8). No close-up on a single man during his speech. Cover: the market with the scales plate."
